// A compact block produced by bitcoind itself -- the anchor for the BIP 152
// short-id KAT (our SipHash keys and short ids must reproduce bitcoind's).
//
// Produced 2026-10-25 with /Satoshi:27.0.0/ (protocol 70016) on a
// throwaway regtest node (fresh datadir, private loopback ports
// rpcport=18743/port=18744, connect=0, stopped and removed afterwards; the
// shared regtest rigs were not touched):
//
//   bitcoind -datadir=$D -conf=$D/bitcoin.conf
//     (regtest=1 server=1 [regtest] port=18744 bind=127.0.0.1 listen=1 fallbackfee=0.0002 maxtxfee=100 dnsseed=0 connect=0 listenonion=0)
//   bitcoin-cli createwallet vec
//   A=$(bitcoin-cli getnewaddress "" bech32)
//   bitcoin-cli generatetoaddress 110 $A
//   six sendtoaddress to fresh addresses: 1.5 (bech32), 2.25 (bech32), 0.75 (legacy), 3.1 (p2sh-segwit), 0.42 (bech32), 5.0 (legacy)
//     (every one spends a segwit coinbase, so every non-coinbase tx has a
//      witness and wtxid != txid)
//   bitcoin-cli generatetoaddress 1 $A      -> the block below
//   bitcoin-cli getblockheader <hash> false / getblock <hash> 0 / getblock <hash> 2
// then a stdlib python P2P client (tools/bip152/capture_cmpct_vector.py:
// version 70016, services NETWORK|WITNESS, verack) sent, on two connections:
//   kCmpctV2Hex:    sendcmpct(false, 2) then getdata(MSG_CMPCT_BLOCK=4, hash)
//   kCmpctV2HbHex:  sendcmpct(true, 2)  then getdata(MSG_CMPCT_BLOCK=4, hash)
// and saved each "cmpctblock" payload verbatim (bitcoind services 0xc09).
// The two payloads are byte-identical: bitcoind served its cached most-recent compact block (same nonce) on both connections.
//
// Do not hand-edit: generated by tools/bip152/emit_fixture.py from
// btc_regtest_cmpct_vector.json (verified by verify_cmpct_vector.py).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

